  "output": {
    "answer": "That's a fair challenge, and the record backs it up: Dez isn't a human tester, it's a fixed-viewport persona simulation, so 30 to 9 seconds is a model scoring its own output, not a usability measurement. That's exactly why the gate still failed — the panel said DONE at 21:50, and on my own iPhone the next morning it was pretty much unusable, three scrolling sections, a help modal on every task, rotating the phone to reach options. So the number tells you the panel's opinion of itself improved; it's necessary as a fast filter, but my own hands on the real device stayed the last gate.",
